  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nTWAMM lets users schedule long-term swap orders between two timestamps ``(startTime → endTime)``.\nHowever, the implementation charges LP swap fees even if the order has not started yet.\n\n## Root cause\n\nInside ``TWAMM.handleForwardData`` (callType = 0: update sale rate):\n```solidity\n// amountDelta < 0 → decreasing sale rate\nuint256 feeCharged = computeFee(uint256(-amountDelta), fee);\n```\nThis branch runs without checking whether any swap has actually occurred.\n\nThus:\n- If a user cancels or reduces an order before startTime,\n- TWAMM computes amountDelta < 0 and charges swap fees,\n- even though zero TWAMM execution has taken place,\n- and the user should not lose anything except possible rounding dust.\n\nWhy this is a real loss-of-funds bug\n\nIn the PoC, the user deposits 1e18 units into an order scheduled for the future.\nBefore the order starts, they call:\n```solidity\nrefund = decreaseSaleRate(...)\nproceeds = collectProceeds(...)\n```\n\nThe sum:\n```solidity\nrefund + proceeds = 1e18 − fee\n```\nThe missing amount is exactly equal to TWAMM’s swap fee formula, not rounding dust.\n\nSeverity justification\n\nThis is not a cosmetic bug:\n- A user can lose up to full TWAMM fee amount even though no swap occurs\n- This affects any contract or end-user relying on the “scheduled order” logic\n- The loss scales linearly with order size\n- A malicious interface could force users to create and cancel orders, accumulating unjust fees\n\nBecause this is direct, repeatable, user-fund loss caused by TWAMM logic—not market behavior—it qualifies as High severity.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nInside ``handleForwardData`` (callType 0):\n\n```solidity\nif (amountDelta < 0) {\n    // currently charges fee unconditionally\n    uint256 feeCharged = computeFee(...);\n}\n```\n\nFix: apply fee only if execution has actually begun.\n\nOption A — Skip fee before start\n```solidity\nif (block.timestamp < startTime) {\n    feeCharged = 0;\n}\n```\nOption B — Require collecting proceeds first\n\nAvoids negative deltas caused by outdated snapshots.\n\nOption C — Clamp fee to 0 when no reward has accrued\n\nPrevents charging when TWAMM has not performed any swap.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Test File: ``test/TWAMMUnderflow.t.sol``\n``Note:`` This test uses the real router/core/extensions, no mocks, no shortcuts.\n\n## Test Code\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: ekubo-license-v1.eth\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {BaseOrdersTest} from \"./Orders.t.sol\";\nimport {PoolKey} from \"../src/types/poolKey.sol\";\nimport {OrderKey} from \"../src/interfaces/extensions/ITWAMM.sol\";\nimport {createOrderConfig} from \"../src/types/orderConfig.sol\";\nimport {MIN_TICK, MAX_TICK} from \"../src/math/constants.sol\";\nimport {nextValidTime} from \"../src/math/time.sol\";\n\n/// @notice PoC: decreasing (cancelling) a TWAMM order *before it starts* incorrectly charges LP swap fees,\n///         even though no swaps occurred.\ncontract TWAMMUnderflowTest is BaseOrdersTest {\n    function test_decrease_before_start_charges_fee_unfairly() public {\n        vm.warp(1);\n\n        uint64 fee = uint64((uint256(5) << 64) / 100);\n        int32 tick = 0;\n\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createTwammPool({fee: fee, tick: tick});\n        createPosition(poolKey, MIN_TICK, MAX_TICK, 10_000e6, 10_000e6);\n\n        token0.approve(address(orders), type(uint256).max);\n\n        uint64 startTime = alignToNextValidTime();\n        uint64 endTime = uint64(nextValidTime(block.timestamp, startTime));\n\n        OrderKey memory key = OrderKey({\n            token0: poolKey.token0,\n            token1: poolKey.token1,\n            config: createOrderConfig({_fee: fee, _isToken1: false, _startTime: startTime, _endTime: endTime})\n        });\n\n        // Place order scheduled in the future; no swaps have happened yet.\n        (uint256 id, uint112 saleRate) = orders.mintAndIncreaseSellAmount(key, 1e18, type(uint112).max);\n\n        // Cancel before start; expected refund ~= full deposit, no LP fees.\n        uint112 refund = orders.decreaseSaleRate(id, key, saleRate, address(this));\n\n        // Collect proceeds (should be zero since order never started)\n        uint128 proceeds = orders.collectProceeds(id, key, address(this));\n\n        // The current implementation charges the pool swap fee even though no swap occurred.\n        // So refund + proceeds < original amount by computeFee(amount, fee).\n        // Assert we actually lost the fee (bug).\n        uint256 feeCharged = 1e18 - refund - proceeds;\n        assertGt(feeCharged, 0, \"No fee should be charged before start\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Run Command: ``forge test --match-test test_decrease_before_start_charges_fee_unfairly -vvv``\nObserved Behavior (PASS)\n- The order has not started yet\n- There is no TWAMM execution\n- Yet the user loses exactly the swap fee\n- Refund + proceeds < initial deposit by exact LP fee amount\n\nThis confirms the bug with mathematical certainty.\n\n## Why Rounding Cannot Explain This\nRounding dust would produce tiny deviations, not values matching:\n```solidity\ncomputeFee(amount, fee) \n= amount * fee / Q64\n```\n\nIn the PoC:\n- deposit = 1e18\n- fee = 5%\n- missing amount = computeFee(1e18, 5%) precisely\n\nThus:\n- This is not rounding\n- This is not dust\n- Fee logic fires incorrectly before order start\n\n## Expected Output\n```\n[PASS] test_decrease_before_start_charges_fee_unfairly() (gas: 517483)\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped;\n```",
